# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING IN THIS DIRECTORY MAY CONTAIN A WORD OF THE MEETING.
#
# The clips are slices of a real private recording. Three classes of file here
# can leak its content, and all three are excluded:
#
#   clips/        audio of real people saying real things
#   references/   a human transcript of the above, plus diarization and
#                 word timings
#   hypotheses/   what the system thought was said
#
# The clips are already covered by the root `.gitignore`'s `*.wav` rule, and
# that is not enough on its own: a `.wav` rule does not cover a `.txt`. Every
# rule below is stated explicitly so the exclusions are auditable by reading
# this file rather than by reasoning about the root one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

clips/
references/
hypotheses/

# The per-frame acoustic analysis is a dense map of the whole recording. The
# *summary* of it (counts, dB percentiles, pause positions) is committed in
# set.json and metadata/; the frames are not.
**/*.frames.json

# Only aggregate reports are committable. `results/` is ignored wholesale and
# then re-admitted file by file, so a new artefact type has to be added here on
# purpose rather than swept in by accident.
results/*
!results/summary.json
!results/*.report.json

# Scratch space for anyone working the set by hand.
evaluation-scratch/
*.local.json
